## Model card

- **Name:** Crouton Alpha (stealth model — maker undisclosed)
- **Short description:** A free, anonymous, lightweight "worker" model pitched at the small repeated steps inside AI agents — coding sub-tasks, tool use, and document/vision analysis rather than long freeform chat. Surfaced on OpenRouter 2026-11-03 (01:38 UTC) under a code name; OpenRouter states it is not the developer/owner/provider.
- **Provider / access:** OpenRouter `stealth/crouton-alpha` (OpenAI-compatible API; free models capped 20 req/min, 50/day, or 1,000/day after ≥$10 credits). Also OpenCode Zen "Crouton Alpha Free" (free week from 3 Nov, output capped ~270,000 tokens/req), Command Code, Kilo Code. No EU in-region routing.
- **Release / knowledge:** Listed 2026-11-03; knowledge cutoff not published. Ranked #2 in OpenRouter new-and-trending on 4 Nov (25.1B tokens processed).
- **IDs:** `stealth/crouton-alpha` (OpenRouter); `opencode/crouton-alpha` (Zen). No first-party vendor ID (maker anonymous).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens (1M) total; max output 943,718 tokens (Zen caps output ~270K/req). Confirmed via OpenRouter API/model page (4 Nov). No long-context retrieval benchmark (MRCR/RULER) published.
- **Modalities:** Input = text, image, file, audio, video (multimodal); Output = text only. Reasoning always on (adjustable minimal→max, defaults to highest effort). Tool calling + structured outputs supported, but `tool_choice` is limited to `auto` (cannot force a specific tool). No image/audio generation.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-09):** $0 per 1M input and output during the preview (free); no announced end date. Precedent: earlier stealth models stopped being free once the maker was named.
- **Architecture:** Undisclosed; "lightweight" worker class. Speed ~2s to first token, ~72 tokens/s (median). No confirmed parameter count. Maker speculation points to Meta's Muse family (matching reasoning-effort levels, a shared rare-Japanese-word failure, and 1,048,576/943,718 limits identical to Muse Spark 1.3), but the same tracker notes token counts don't match Meta, and a tokenizer probe ruled out Google, Qwen, Mistral and GLM — lineage UNCONFIRMED.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SELF-EXCLUSION: zero verified public benchmark numbers were found for this
> exact model/ID — every standard row below reads "no verified public score
> found." Per `tasks/research.md` rule 9 + template SELF-EXCLUSION, no scored
> `.md` is written and no placeholder scores are invented.

Agent / tool use:

- Terminal-Bench / Tau-Bench / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas / GDPval-AA: **no verified public score found**. Qualitative only: a MindStudio hands-on (Hermes sub-agent harness) had it split a 3-task coding plan across fresh sub-agents, pass spec + quality review, and produce code that passed all 20 tests on independent re-run — a pass/fail demo, not a standardized tool-use benchmark score.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond / HLE / LCR / MLCR / CritPt: **no verified public score found**.
- Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: **not tracked** — `artificialanalysis.ai/models/crouton-alpha` returns HTTP 404.
- BenchLM overall: **not tracked** — `benchlm.ai/models/crouton-alpha` returns HTTP 404.
- Qualitative only: MindStudio reported it read a dense wind-tunnel poster and correctly flagged real faults (inconsistent Reynolds/Mach numbers, wrong stall-angle/CL-max units, one invalid equation) without hints — strong document reasoning, but no numeric score.

Coding:

- SWE-bench Verified / LiveCodeBench / HumanEval / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench: **no verified public score found**.
- One X tester reported 140 of 157 tasks passed on a personal test set with "a perfect coding score and a weaker result in maths" — per i-scoop this is "a single person's benchmark and a first impression, not a ranking" (not fetched in full, not a first-party/dedicated host) → does not qualify as a verified public score.

Long context:

- 1,048,576-token window confirmed via the OpenRouter API, but **no long-context retrieval benchmark reported** (no MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks score).

Multimodal:

- Text/image/file/audio/video input confirmed via the OpenRouter API; **no multimodal benchmark score found**. Qualitative: MindStudio's vision test converted a hand-drawn sketch with handwritten notes ("spin slowly", "slices fall here") into a working animated single-file HTML page in ~3 min; multilingual output was uneven (strong on major languages, wrong on Kurdish/Odia).

> Provenance & meta verification:
> - `model/crouton-alpha/meta.json` states "Text in/out only" — CONTRADICTED by the OpenRouter API/model page (input = text, image, file, audio, video; output = text only). The context figure (1,048,576 / 943,718) and free-tier pricing match. Premise-corrected the modality above on the fresh OpenRouter evidence — recommend the orchestrator fix `modalities` in meta.json.
> - Maker identity is unconfirmed (Meta/Muse-family speculation vs. tokenizer counter-evidence); do not treat lineage as fact.

